never mind  after President Vladimir Putin mobilized  ordinary Russians to fight in Ukraine in  September large protests broke out  families mourn conscripts who died on  the front lines and hundreds of  thousands of Russian men fled the  country  but these are the images that Russians  are seeing on state media  National Television showed the president  firing a rifle and inspecting  preservists who looked all set to fight  and citizens say on air they are fully  prepared for combat  as Putin faces a backlash against  immobilization here's how the state  propaganda machine has stepped in to try  to reassure the population  when the mobilization was announced  State tv reported that men were flocking  to recruitment centers out of patriotism  and it showed smiling families sending  their loved ones to war the Russian army  said it was drafting ordinary citizens  to help hold the front lines in Ukraine  and Ankara said the population responded  with a wave of support  those reports came as recruitment  centers were being targeted by a series  of attacks and polls showed growing  anxiety among Russians  according to an independent pollster the  number of Russians who think that the  campaign in Ukraine is going as planned  dropped to 53 percent of September from  73 in May  days after announcing the mobilization  Putin admitted that the way the draft  was managed raised many questions  but in October the kremlins start to  face criticism as new recruits start on  the front lines just days after being  summoned some families say they were  poorly trained  foreign  about equipment shortages saying they  had to buy things such as flashlights or  sleeping bags themselves  so news reports start to regularly cover  those themes mobilize men going through  battle drills dressed in mint condition  uniforms and equipped with all the gear  needed for combat helmets bulletproof  vests and sleeping bags  and the president himself went on camera  and gave a word of encouragement to the  new draftees  noise  it's hard to tell how effective the  state propaganda is according to border  authorities in Europe and other  countries more than 300 000 Russians  have left the territory since late  September many say they fled to avoid  being sent to war  still many Russians expressed strong  support for the invasion of Ukraine and  are not averse to the mobilization  foreign foreign  the Kremlin said that even though there  were problems of the mobilization the  situation shouldn't be generalized  according to Putin reservists can be  sent to the front lines after 10 to 25  days of training  in late October handout footage from the  Russian government showed Russia's  Minister of Defense telling Putin that  the mobilization was successfully  concluding with some 300 000 men drafted  however many Russians say they are  skeptical the president didn't sign an  official decree to end the draft saying  it wasn't necessary  this has fueled concerns that the  mobilization could resume at any moment  as Russia continues to suffer setbacks  in Ukraine
 

